<div class="max-w-[960px] mx-auto">
  {% include "page-header.njk" %}

  <div class="flex items-end gap-3 mb-2" id="picker-tabs-row">
    <climbing-discipline-picker></climbing-discipline-picker>
    <climbing-tab-bar active-page="performance"></climbing-tab-bar>
  </div>

  <a class="back-link mt-4 mb-5" id="back-to-performance-link" href="#">
    <svg class="w-[.9rem] h-[.9rem] stroke-current fill-none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"></path><path d="M19 12H5"></path></svg>
    Performance Insights
  </a>

  <h1 class="page-title">Volume / Intensity</h1>

  <div class="mb-5" id="view-explainer">
    <p class="text-[.95rem] text-foreground leading-[1.7]">How much you're climbing and how hard, together — send count and peak grade by time period.</p>
    <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted leading-[1.7] mt-2">Bars are climbs logged per period; the overlaid line marks the toughest grade sent that period, labeled directly on its points. Built from every logged <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold">send</strong>'s grade -- a send-log proxy for training load, not a measure of real training stimulus (this app has no visibility into gym or hangboard training).</p>
  </div>

  <div class="row-card text-center max-w-[420px] mx-auto" id="performance-offline" hidden>
    <p class="text-[.9rem] text-foreground">Performance insights need a connection.</p>
    <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted mt-2">Reconnect and reload this page to see your volume/intensity trend.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
    <div id="time-window-root"></div>
    <div id="report-grade-scale-root"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="trends-root"></div>

  <h2 class="sources-heading">Sources</h2>
  <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted leading-[1.7] mb-3">Varying training load over time (periodization) is standard climbing-coaching practice, but no peer-reviewed source validates "sends per period" specifically as a training-load metric -- this view is a send-log-derived proxy for volume/intensity balance, not a measurement of actual training stimulus.</p>
  <ol class="m-0 pl-[1.2rem] text-[.84rem] leading-[1.6] text-foreground [&>li+li]:mt-[10px]">
    <li>Bechtel, S., Stewart, K., Snavely, Z., Ratz, M., &amp; Watt, J. <em class="text-muted italic">Logical Progression: Using Nonlinear Periodization for Year-Round Climbing Performance</em>. Argues climbing's demands are acyclic, favoring non-linear periodization over strict sequential blocks -- the coaching basis for tracking volume and intensity together rather than as separate, independently-optimized numbers.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="text-center text-muted text-[.78rem] mt-8" id="footer"></div>
</div>
